Competitive Landscape
Google (Alphabet Inc.) continues to dominate the ecosystem, leveraging its unified data assets across Search, YouTube, and the Google Display Network. Meta Platforms commands a sizable share of social mediated ad spend, while Amazon Advertising is reshaping the value chain by targeting shoppers at the point of purchase. In Asia, Alibaba’s Alimama and Tencent’s WeChat advertising solidify regional dominance, and Baidu remains the primary search advertising player in China. Mid size and niche players such as Verizon Media (Yahoo), Snap Inc., Pinterest, Taboola, Outbrain, Microsoft (LinkedIn Ads), and Roku Advertising provide specialized formats and vertical expertise that broaden the market’s tactical options.
